ernance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["AnaptysBio, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.4B market cap on $235M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +184% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +38.5pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -127% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $20M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 15% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 5.6% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (37.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries a 996% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":9.9571197933484},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2497021.67},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): roic below cost of capital; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 36% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Healthcare \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Where Does AnaptysBio (ANAB) Valuation Sit On Its Latest Earnings Reset?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-anab/anaptysbio/news/where-does-anaptysbio-anab-valuation-sit-on-its-latest-earni","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794558260.055,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.867,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"AnaptysBio, Inc. (ANAB) Misses Q3 Earnings and Revenue Estimates","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/anaptysbio-inc-anab-misses-q3-220502